==English==
{{wikipedia|Heim (surname)}}

===Etymology===
* As a south {{der|en|de|-}} surname, from the noun {{m|de|Heim|t=home}}.
* As a {{der|en|no|-}} surname, from farmsteads named with, or directly from, the {{der|en|non|-}} noun {{m|non|heimr|t=home}}, related to the above.
* As a Jewish surname, from the {{der|en|yi|-}} name {{m|yi|חיים|tr=Khayem}}. {{doublet|en|Chaim}}.

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|s}}

# {{surname|en|from=German}}.

====Statistics====
* According to the 2010 United States Census, ''Heim'' is the 2513<sup>th</sup> most common surname in the United States, belonging to 14414 individuals. ''Heim'' is most common among White (91.66%) individuals.

